<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened Runtime exceptions for the notarised MediFlow build.

  Notarisation requires the Hardened Runtime (codesign "options runtime"), and
  the Hardened Runtime breaks a PyInstaller + PySide6 app unless these three are
  granted. Each one is here because the app does not start without it, not as a
  precaution:

  * allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory: CPython writes and then
    executes memory it generated itself, and Qt's regex and QML engines do the
    same.
  * disable-library-validation: a PyInstaller one-dir bundle loads dozens of Qt
    frameworks and C extension .so files at runtime. Library validation refuses
    any library not signed by the same team, and these come out of the PySide6
    and cryptography wheels.

  None of this weakens the sealing of the field-encryption key: a Keychain ACL
  is bound to the signed binary, and that binary is still signed and verified.

  Deliberately NOT granted, so reach for one only against a real launch failure:
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables,
  com.apple.security.cs.debugger, and every com.apple.security.device.* key.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
